  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "On November 21, 2026, volcanic activity was reported at two prominent Indonesian sites, Mount Semeru in East Java and Mount Ibu in North Maluku. Reports indicate that both volcanoes ejected ash columns rising hundreds of meters into the atmosphere. The events follow a period of intermittent activity at Mount Semeru, which has experienced multiple eruptions throughout November. Officials are currently monitoring the volcanic output and have issued warnings for the surrounding populations to exercise caution. While Mount Semeru has seen frequent seismic and volcanic fluctuations in recent weeks, these latest eruptions are part of a broader period of heightened geological activity observed across various Indonesian mountains during the same timeframe. Residents and visitors are instructed to adhere to safety protocols, including the suspension of climbing activities in the affected areas as government geological monitoring continues.",
